meta {
  name: Update Project
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/project/updateProject/{{projectId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Renamed project",
    "frontEndTech": ["Next.js", "Tailwind"]
  }
}

docs {
  # Update Project

  Admin only. JSON, not multipart — **the image cannot be replaced here**; delete
  and recreate the project instead.

  Partial by design: only the keys you send change. Unknown keys (`id`, `image`,
  `createdAt`, `updatedAt`) are stripped by the schema, which doubles as the
  mass-assignment whitelist. Unlike Create, the tech lists are real JSON arrays.

  | Status | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | 200 | updated |
  | 401 | missing or expired token |
  | 404 | `NOT_FOUND` |
  | 409 | `DUPLICATE_KEY` — that `slug` belongs to another project |
  | 422 | `VALIDATION_ERROR` — e.g. an empty `frontEndTech` |

  Sending a link as `""` clears it. `backEndTech` may be `[]`; `frontEndTech` may
  not, since every project has a frontend.

  `slug` is editable but never moves on its own: renaming the title leaves the
  existing URL alone, and sending `slug: ""` is a no-op rather than a reset.

  `status` and `order` can be set here too, though **Toggle Published** is the
  usual way to flip the gate.
}
